Generate the autocompletion script for the bash shell.

This script depends on the 'bash-completion' package.
If it is not installed already, you can install it via your OS's package
manager.

To load completions in your current shell session:

        source <(cron-person completion bash)

To load completions for every new session, execute once:

#### Linux:

        cron-person completion bash > /etc/bash_completion.d/cron-person

#### macOS:

        cron-person completion bash > $(brew
        --prefix)/etc/bash_completion.d/cron-person

You will need to start a new shell for this setup to take effect.

Usage:
  cron-person completion bash

Flags:
  -h, --help              help for bash
      --no-descriptions   disable completion descriptions

Global Flags:
      --config string   Path to custom configuration file (default:
                        $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cron-person/config.json)
      --store string    Path to custom authorization state file (default:
                        $XDG_STATE_HOME/cron-person/allowed.json)
